theorem: for all n in N, 2 * (sum from i=1 to n of i) = n(n + 1)
proof
we proceed by induction on n.
base case n = 0: sum from i=1 to 0 of i = 0
inductive step: assume 2 * (sum from i=1 to k of i) = k(k + 1).
then 2 * (sum from i=1 to k+1 of i) = k(k + 1) + 2(k + 1) = (k + 1)(k + 2)
qed
